# Implementation Plan

## Scenario 1 - Room Setup & Lobby (Complete)

## Scenario 2 - Game Start & Drawer Flow

### Discovery Notes
- **Gaps identified:**
  - `RoomStatus` only has `lobby`. Needs `playing`.
  - `Room` model lacks `currentWord`, `drawerId`, and `round` info.
  - `RoomSnapshot` doesn't filter `currentWord` based on the viewer's role.
  - No `POST /rooms/:code/start` endpoint.
- **Assumptions:**
  - Deterministic word selection means taking the first word for the first round.

### State Model Changes
#### Backend
- `backend/src/models/game.ts`:
  - `RoomStatus`: Add `playing`.
  - `Room`: Add `drawerId?: string`, `secretWord?: string`.
  - `RoomSnapshot`: Add `secretWord?: string`, `isDrawer: boolean`.

### Data Flow
- **Start Game**: `POST /rooms/:code/start` (Host only) -> Backend sets status to `playing`, assigns `drawerId` (host), and picks `secretWord`.
- **Sync**: All players polling `GET /rooms/:code` see status `playing` and redirect to `/game`.
- **Word Visibility**: `toRoomSnapshot` only includes `secretWord` if `viewerParticipantId === room.drawerId`.

### File-level Changes
- `backend/src/models/game.ts`: Update types.
- `backend/src/services/roomStore.ts`: Add `startGame` function.
- `backend/src/api/rooms.ts`: Add `POST /:code/start` route.
- `frontend/src/pages/LobbyPage.tsx`: Redirect when status is `playing`.
- `frontend/src/pages/GamePage.tsx`: Display word for drawer, hide for others.

### Risks
- Ensuring all players redirect simultaneously (polling latency might cause slight delay).
- Role assignment logic needs to be robust.
